{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug Phase 1 RCA (confirmed at runtime).\n\nMechanism: impact-present close -> close_precheck._check_work_landed -> commit_impact.referencing_commits, which walks all code history and resolves every extracted historical candidate via resolve_ticket_id. The prior alias-index fix (commit 5c64deff, ticket 4234-821b) bounded ONLY the alias branch: build_alias_index runs one store pass and resolve_ticket_id(alias_index=...) does an in-memory lookup for aliases. The RESIDUAL is the two other resolution branches in src/rebar/_ids.py:resolve_ticket_id that still call os.listdir(tracker_dir) once PER candidate:\n - the 8-hex short-id branch (_SHORT_ID_RE; matches[...] over os.listdir when no exact dir), and\n - the generic prefix branch (len>=4; n.startswith(ticket_id) over os.listdir).\nOrdinary subject prefixes, deprecated 4-digit fragments, and short-id-shaped tokens that name no dir all fall through the alias_index (which returns [] for a non-alias) into these two branches, so each unique historical candidate drives a fresh full tracker-root listing -> O(unique_candidates x tracker) directory listings before completion verification. This is the impact-present 'history x tracker' scaling the ticket names.\n\nRuntime proof: a synthetic repo with a target credited by alias plus 80 distinct non-alias candidate trailers (40 short-id-shaped, 40 four-digit) recorded 82 tracker-root os.listdir scans during referencing_commits (1 index build + one per candidate), target still correctly credited. Falsifiable prediction held: had only the alias path been the cost, scans would be <=1; instead they scaled linearly with candidates.\n\nRivals rejected: (a) 'alias-index already fixed it' — refuted, aliases ARE bounded but short-id/prefix are not; (b) 'os.listdir is negligible' — it is a full tracker-root listing (5.3k entries) per candidate, i.e. exactly the walk AC#1 forbids and the mechanism the pre-5c64deff 25-62m telemetry sampled (the alias JSON-read cost has since been removed, leaving this listing cost).\n\nLegitimacy: defect. AC#1/#2 require bounded work; the current short-id/prefix branches perform a full tracker walk per candidate.\n\nOrigin: the impact-present close landing scan that resolves arbitrary historical candidates was introduced by 746c1ba2e961 'Add attach-commits verb and impact-vs-diff gate' (ticket cec6-0a0e-38a9-4234); the alias sub-case was later partially bounded by 4234-821b, leaving the short-id/prefix residual. Phase 2 (RED-first) unlocked."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787552009347647001,"uuid":"f5acb3f2-193c-4c9e-a19d-0c7ba86ce7e4"}